    <briefdescription>
<para>A raw PCM sample that can be pitch-shifted when played by a track. data: mono signed PCM in the given format. num_bytes: size of data in bytes. format: sample rate + bit depth (see <ref refid="group___speaker_1gaf647901e7f8ebfaa0f41f433cec0b1cf" kindref="member">SpeakerPcmFormat</ref>). base_midi_note: the MIDI note at which the sample plays unshifted (e.g. 60 = C4). Notes above/below this value are produced by resampling. loop: if true, the sample restarts from the beginning each time it runs out, and keeps playing until the owning note&apos;s duration elapses. </para>
    </briefdescription>
